{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Man.</b> Rabbi Judah HaLevi said: [the verse] 'like sheep they are laid in Sheol' — [meaning] a man with honor will not lodge [overnight]; the interpretation is that he will not sleep and die, and this is the honor of the soul. Likewise, a man who has not learned will not understand; therefore he is like the beasts."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:20.087961910Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}